extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski printed 115-120 (cache p115-p120, cache page = printed folio + 0 for printed 38-177), a text layer. The manifest lists none of these pages as welded, corrupt or digit-substituted; printed 116 is a full-page illustration with no text. Printed 119 (the Cyber-Humanoid M.D.C. by Location, damage and leg figures) and the ladder on printed 224 were read off renders and agree with the cache. Heading Spetsnaz Intel O.C.C., Intelligence Division/KGB Agent (printed 115); stats Spetsnaz Intelligence Officer Stats (printed 117). A Red Army special forces and intelligence officer beside the other Sovietski military O.C.C.s, so occ_group men-of-arms and men_of_arms true. || XP: the ladder headed Spetsnaz/Special Forces in the Experience Tables (printed 224, cache p220). || BRANCH: SVR, OVPUB or KGB, a pick-one ability group; each branch''s identities, contacts, skills and the OVPUB P.P.E. or I.S.P. are prose, because a chosen ability grants no skills and the pool applies only to a mage or psychic. || SKILLS: Contacts is the catalog''s Contacts - Social Connections. Pilot: Hover Craft (Ground) is Hover Craft (ground). Hand to Hand: Martial Arts is granted and no other style is sold, so costs is empty; Commando or Assassin comes in the M.O.S. bundles that print it, as a grant that replaces it. || M.O.S.: one bundle in place of O.C.C. Related Skills, each with a Training ability carrying its bonuses (the Sovietski Soldier''s shape). This script holds the five whose text ends by printed 120: Airborne Deployment Specialist, Commando, Cyber-Humanoid, Electronic Intelligence and Guerilla Warfare/Saboteur. The skill bonuses each prints to the O.C.C. Skills (Intelligence, Radio: Basic, Surveillance, Tailing, Computer Operation) are prose. Airborne prints +10% to Intelligence twice in one sentence; both are recorded in its Training. Pilot: Military Helicopter is Military: Combat Helicopter; Pilot: Jet Pack is Jet Packs; Tracking (Humanoids) is Tracking (people). In Commando, the +20% beside Motorcycles and Snowmobiles is read as that option''s only. A one-of-two attribute pick (P.E. or P.P.) is prose. || CYBER-HUMANOID: no vessel row exists for the body, so the main body (112) is the Training''s mdc_base and the rest of the M.D.C. by Location and its bionics are prose, citing catalog slugs where a row exists. No row was found for the Multi-System Hand, Cyber-Disguise AA-1 or ASH, Psionic Electromagnetic Dampeners, Modulating Voice Synthesizer, Cyber-Camera Eye or Bio-System Nightvision Eyes. || MONEY: no savings stated, so no starting_money; the salary and lodging are in restrictions. || EQUIPMENT: the pocket-sized silver cross signal mirror is stored as a small silver cross and a signal mirror, as the Sovietski Soldier reads the same line. Not stored as rows: listed in restrictions."
